Human gameplay and release validation:
    Scope: current code as of 2026-10-09; European title 00040000000A5F00, CTR-P-AG5P.
    This checklist is not a claim that the full randomizer is playable. Source extraction and compilation are not gameplay evidence.
    All unchecked tasks need a person's observation. Code/unit/Lua checks are tracked separately in PATCH_TODO.md.
    @critical = run before a long playthrough; @coverage = repeat for every listed identity; @blocked = implementation/evidence prerequisite.
    Record seed, settings, catalog hash, patch fingerprint, build revision, emulator/version, language, save slot and expected placement.
    Keep notes/reproduction steps below a failing entry. Mark done only for the configuration actually observed.
    Use user-generated fixtures and disposable save slots. Keep backups for rollback, cross-seed and interrupted-save tests.
    Individual hook fixtures may grant traversal tools for reaching a test target; they do not prove a shuffled seed is solvable.
    For critical cases test a fresh save, room re-entry, in-session load, emulator restart, and loading the saved slot again.
    Do not copy a passing emulator/version/language result to an untested combination.

Previously confirmed human observations (old revision-2 tutorial fixture only):
    ✔ Arrival at Decalburg and the unrolling event worked; user confirmed on 2026-10-08.
    ✔ The old fixture showed four Jump, four Hammer and two Mushroom stickers; user confirmed on 2026-10-08.
    ✔ Movement resumed after unrolling; user confirmed on 2026-10-08.
    These observations do not validate the current production startup, shuffled abilities, current seeds or save/reload.

Preparation and supported builds:
    ☐ Record exact ROM identity, emulator/version, build revision, language and the fixture's settings before each test group. @critical
    ☐ Load a user-generated mod by itself; confirm an older LayeredFS mod is not masking current files. @critical
    ☐ Install the generated romfs and exefs overrides together and verify the client recognizes their executable signature. @critical
    ☐ Test the packaged CLI and GUI on Windows using paths containing spaces and non-ASCII characters. @release
    ☐ Test the Linux packages on the declared x86-64/glibc baseline, including launch permissions and compiler paths. @release
    ☐ Test each emulator/version/platform before advertising it; record unsupported combinations explicitly. @release
    ☐ Confirm a wrong title, encrypted/incompatible dump or mismatched recipe produces a useful error and leaves prior mods intact. @release
    ☐ Confirm generating to existing recipe/tracker outputs preserves those files; invalid registry input creates no new seed recipe. @release
    ☐ Confirm applying to an existing mod directory preserves it and refuses replacement. @release
    ☐ Confirm packaged patch supports generate-native-catalog and apply, and external compilation does not open a visible console window. @release
    ☐ Confirm the GUI can invoke catalog survey/bind and native patch commands; error and success text remains readable. @release
    ☐ Confirm the APWorld installer targets custom_worlds, replacement confirmation works, and the intended demo/native world is loaded. @release
    ☐ Verify distributable recipes, tracker packs and APWorlds contain no ROM bytes, decompiled game scripts or original game artwork. @release

Production startup and ability ownership:
    ☐ Start a fresh seed: intro bypass reaches the world map without hanging or leaving Mario/UI control disabled. @critical
    ☐ Confirm Decalburg is already unrolled, rescued Toads are initialized, and tutorial Goombas are gone. @critical
    ☐ Confirm no tutorial battle, forced rescue or unrolling scene starts again on re-entry or save/load. @critical
    ☐ With Hammer unowned, hammer input cannot break progression obstacles and no hardcoded Hammer/copies are granted. @critical
    ☐ Receive Hammer, then verify actual hammer input, obstacle effects and persistence after saving/restarting. @critical
    ☐ With Paperization unowned, its input/UI and puzzle/door interactions remain unavailable. @critical
    ☐ Receive Paperization, then verify actual entry/exit controls, cancellation, return to movement and save/reload. @critical
    ☐ The album accessory remains usable when Hammer and Paperization are both unowned. @critical
    ☐ Compare empty, Hammer-only, Paperization-only and both-ability starting inventories; only configured abilities are owned. @critical
    ☐ All configured starting rewards arrive once; re-entry and AP echoes do not add extra copies or capabilities. @critical
    ☐ Starting stickers that cannot fit remain pending and retry after capacity is freed, without forced insertion or loss. @critical
    ☐ Re-enter the startup room after a saved start with pending rewards; delivery still retries before the normal entry path. @critical
    ☐ Keep Decalburg's access item unowned while visiting an accessible other stage: Menu-to-Decalburg admission stays blocked. @critical
    ☐ Receive Decalburg access: enter via every normal world-map/return route without bypassing other native requirements. @critical
    ☐ Repeat town admission with production skips disabled when using a fixture that supports that configuration. @critical

Language and presentation matrix:
    ☐ English: fresh opening, dialogue, supported boss intros and all five Royal intermissions complete with control restored. @critical
    ☐ French: repeat the English presentation cases and retain required flags/rewards. @language
    ☐ German: repeat the English presentation cases and retain required flags/rewards. @language
    ☐ Italian: repeat the English presentation cases and retain required flags/rewards. @language
