    ☐ First visits: five Royal-boss intros automatically use their safe skip intervals without skipping required setup. @critical
    ☐ Repeat attempts after escape/loss: those intros still restore camera, NPC and player state correctly. @critical
    ☐ First quiz-show intro: automatic skip reaches the quiz; choice menus, prizes and scoring still work. @gameplay
    ☐ Every supported scene's cleanup handles active message/effect threads without a stuck camera or orphaned actor. @gameplay
    ☐ Each Royal intermission returns through its original exit and restores the book, hands/buttons and normal field control. @critical
    ☐ With pages randomized, intermissions and the 1-3 Toad add no vanilla page upgrade. @critical
    ☐ With Royals shuffled, a boss/intermission adds no vanilla Royal ownership even when its assigned prize is filler. @critical
    ☐ With either skip setting disabled, the original relevant sequence remains available and its configured reward suppression still applies. @gameplay
    ☐ Ordinary dialogue skip handling preserves seen flags and all surrounding quest effects. @gameplay
    ☐ Shop purchase/sale choices, quiz choices, save confirmation and other interactive menus remain usable. @critical
    ☐ Inventory-full, error, price and confirmation messages remain understandable and do not leave the game waiting invisibly. @gameplay
    ☐ Observe every remaining story/cutscene family; record the trigger, required effects, cleanup and exact wait that still needs a skip. @catalog
    Universal textbox removal and cutscenes without inspected safe paths are not implemented; record evidence before requesting broader skips.

Reward identity and source separation:
    ☐ Collect a mini star with a filler prize: only the configured prize arrives; the vanilla exit-star capability is not granted. @critical
    ☐ Receive that exit-star reward at another location or from another player: its encoded destination opens without collecting its original source. @critical
    ☐ Alternate exits and shortcuts retain distinct capabilities and open only their configured native route. @gameplay
    ☐ Defeat each boss with filler/remote prizes: its source check completes once without granting its vanilla Royal or shuffled admission item. @critical
    ☐ Receive a Royal before defeating its boss: source visibility, boss trigger and story progression still function. @critical
    ☐ Receiving Royal 6 alone or replacing one of Royals 1-5 with Royal 6 never admits the castle. @critical
    ☐ Receive all five distinct Royals 1-5: actual castle traversal succeeds only when its other prerequisites are satisfied. @critical
    ☐ Boss admission locked/unlocked states work for all six Royal bosses and the Harbor boss; native route gates still apply. @gameplay
    ☐ A fixed Event remains at its declared source and observes its original flag rather than an unrelated inventory receipt. @gameplay
    ☐ Intermediate fixed Goals never finish the game; the actual Bowser EndGoal does. @critical
    ☐ Escape/loss from the final fight never reports victory; genuine Bowser victory does, once. @critical

Thing, scrap, peel and chest behavior:
