    ☐ Disabled banners have no check/prize/tracker marker and cannot hold progression or keep the goal unreachable. @critical
    ☐ Already earned banners remain earned after reload without another shuffled prize. @gameplay

Album settings, capacity and receipts:
    ☐ All-at-start: exactly eight usable pages after initialization, no page rewards in the pool, no repeated starting upgrades. @critical
    ☐ Randomized: exactly two base pages; each of six received upgrades adds one usable page independent of Royals and bosses. @critical
    ☐ Verify each capacity from two through eight using actual placement, moving/peeling stickers, menus, battles and purchases. @gameplay
    ☐ Two pages hold all early required simultaneous tools; record exact sticker sizes and any unavoidable capacity gate. @catalog
    ☐ An upgrade received ahead of a blocked remote sticker creates capacity; that sticker then commits once. @critical
    ☐ Independent page/ability/access receipt does not acknowledge or discard the earlier blocked ordered reward. @critical
    ☐ A pending local sticker waits while an incoming page adds space, then commits once without host inventory writes. @critical
    ☐ Full-album repeated retries, room changes and save/restart never force insertion, lose rewards or duplicate receipts. @critical
    ☐ Receiving later idempotent ability/access/Royal capabilities does not mutate album contents or advance the blocked prefix ACK. @gameplay
    ☐ Filling/freeing the scrap album leaves unrelated saved mailbox bytes, seed identity and capability ownership intact. @gameplay
    ☐ Save while several rewards are pending: delivered checks remain delivered, pending ones retry once and new checks still work. @critical
    ☐ Coin filler adds the configured amount up to the game's native cap, without repeated grants or other inventory effects. @gameplay
    ☐ Wrong-seed or incompatible save/patch pairing rejects new grants/check commits without clearing prior inventory or silently rebinding. @critical
    ☐ Native receipts, starting ownership and mailbox identity survive fresh load, application restart and ordinary saves in every used slot. @critical
    Infinite inventory is not implemented/enabled. Do not test it as a supported mode.

