Deferred implementation prerequisites (not passable as current gameplay features):
    Full-game verified traversal/puzzle/event graph is not yet populated; the route/puzzle registers below collect its required evidence.
    Wiggler acquisition/transformations and selected enemy encounter accessibility still require classification and native-hook decisions.
    Universal textbox/cutscene skipping is incomplete; preserve menu choices and required effects when specifying remaining skips.
    Infinite capacity requires bounded storage, menu/battle/shop integration and compatible persistence before human release tests can run.
    General page-capacity logic needs human measurements of sticker geometry and simultaneous puzzle/battle inventory requirements.
    The 416 observed source checks are not proof that every legitimate gameplay source or encounter has been classified.

Observed native source coverage protocol (416 checks):
    Each source entry below needs physical acquisition/trigger, correct assigned prize, no vanilla duplicate, repeat/re-entry and save/restart.
    Repeat representative source categories with filler, local progression, remote ownership and a capacity-blocked reward.
    For enemies, verify every hook variant has a real encounter and shares the correct first-victory receipt; record unavailable variants for catalog revision.
    For museum entries, physically donate the accepted sticker; receipt of that sticker alone must not complete the exhibit.
    Leave unreachable/unclassified entries pending and attach evidence; a native table entry is not a successful gameplay test.

